  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find the reciprocal of a fraction, we switch the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{9}\\,\\to \\,\\frac{9}{4}\n$$\n\nNow, we convert the resulting fraction to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n9÷4=2\\,\\text{R}1=2\\,\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nSo the reciprocal of $\\frac{4}{9}$ is $2\\,\\frac{1}{4}.$",
